;; resources/llm.edn — which fleet model writes dougaka's video plans.
;;
;; This is an EXPLICIT selection (owner, 2026-08-22): the Modal-served
;; `qwen3.8-27b-fastmtp-aggressive` behind the api.murakumo.cloud gateway,
;; not the fleet's `murakumo-main` alias. The alias stays the fleet-wide
;; default and is untouched; this file is what "opting in" looks like for
;; one consumer. Resolution order in dougaka.deploy/resolve-chat-endpoint:
;;   ① env DOUGAKA_LLM_URL / DOUGAKA_LLM_MODEL
;;   ② this file
;;   ③ the murakumo-main alias
;;   ④ endpoint-only fallback
;;
;; Measured 2026-08-22 against this entry: GET /v1/models lists it; one
;; chat completion answered FASTMTP_OK in 19 s including the cold start
;; (Modal scales to zero after 5 min; cold start ~17 s; 95–99 tok/s warm;
;; 32K context). :max-tokens is the plan budget the owner raised from 1024.
;; Measured the same day: the gateway clamps completion at 2048 whatever is
;; asked (max_tokens 4096 → finish=length at exactly 2048), and with
;; reasoning ON 3 of 8 planning calls spent that whole budget thinking and
;; returned no text. So :thinking? is false here — a plan is ~600 tokens and
;; fits with room — and :max-tokens states the intent, not the clamp.
;;
;; Delete this file to fall back to the alias. Set :model to nil to keep the
;; gateway but let the alias choose the model.
{:llm/version 1
 :endpoint "https://api.murakumo.cloud/v1/chat/completions"
 :models-url "https://api.murakumo.cloud/v1/models"
 :model "qwen3.8-27b-fastmtp-aggressive"
 :max-tokens 4096
 :thinking? false
 :chosen-by "owner 2026-08-22 (murakumo PR #323 / local-murakumo PR #141)"}
